The user wants to multiply 17 and 23.

    *   Method 1: Standard multiplication
        17 * 23 = 17 * (20 + 3)
        = (17 * 20) + (17 * 3)
        = 340 + 51
        = 391

    *   Method 2: Difference of squares
        17 * 23 = (20 - 3) * (20 + 3)
        = 20^2 - 3^2
        = 400 - 9
        = 391

    *   Method 3: Long multiplication
          23
        x 17
        ----
         161 (7 * 23)
         230 (10 * 23)
        ----
         391

The result is 391.
